:: Carter House Intro Part 3 [nobr]

/* Intro */
<span style="Color:LightGreen">Despite the embarrassment of accidentally flashing his entire body to both of you, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> quickly gets over it and the two of you enjoy playing in the pool. It is pretty neat having such a large pool to yourself. While it isn’t massive, it does feel pretty big since it is just you two using it. You know your family would probably love a pool like this and mention it as you both swim around.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Yeah! They should come over sometime. Dad loves to barbeque! He makes the best burgers!”</span> He laughs, splashing you, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Though, if we do, promise you’ll remind me to tie my drawstring? You seeing my butt is one thing, but if other people did…”</span> He laughs nervously. <span style="Color:Pink">You laugh that your brothers probably wouldn’t mind seeing his cute butt, which eventually leads to a playful splash battle between you two that</span> is only interrupted as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Mr. Kent</span> whistling at you both as he finishes painting. <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Happy",
            },
        },
        {
            Name: "Carter",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Swim",
                Mouth: "Happy",
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Alright, I’m done here. I’m going to head inside, but I’ll keep the window open to keep an eye on you. Just shout if you need me!”</span> He says, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“And remember the rules, no swimming alone. So, if one of you finishes up, the other has to get out. I’ll grab you both towels for when you’re done, so try not to track water inside, okay?”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Alright! Thanks dad!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> says happily. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Let me know when you’re done and I’ll put the cover back on. But once I do, that’s it for the day. Alright?”</span> He explains as both you and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> nod, going back to playing as he heads inside. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“We can stop swimming whenever you want, Dad normally lets me have friends over until 7, since that’s dinner time and then I have to get ready for bed.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> explains, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“And we don’t have to just swim, we can do whatever.”</span> He points to the other instruments of fun outside in the yard, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Once you’re ready to change back, just let me know, okay?”</span> You nod, continuing to swim around with <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>. <br>
<span style="color:Gold">Memory Unlocked: "Just Another Night"</span> <span style="color:Grey">[Memories can be viewed in the Journal in your Bedroom.]</span><br>
<br>
<span style="color:Grey">[Tutorial: Sometimes, when hanging out in certain locations, NPCs will have <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“States”</span>. This can determine what activities you can do and what events you get. For example, when at <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s House you can enter the <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Swim State”</span>, which changes you both into your swimwear and unlocks the pool. It also will change the events you get when playing outside. However, you can’t go inside when in <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Swim State”</span> outside of a snack or using the bathroom. Once you exit the <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Swim State”</span>, the pool will be closed for the day and you can’t reenter the <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Swim State”</span> until the next day. So, keep that in mind when you decide you are finished. The playdate will end after 7PM regardless of your current state. Normally, when you first come to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s House, you will be in the <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Normal State”</span> and will have to enter the <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Swim State”</span> via the Backyard.]</span> <br>
<<set $ActiveQuests.delete("Carter: First Visit")>>
